mission "The Sailmaker's Son"
    category "side"
    name "The Sailmaker's Son"
    description "Find a runaway sailmaker's apprentice and bring him to Port Azure."
    source "Tortuga"
    destination "Port Azure"
    reward 350
    speaker offer "Madame Celine"
    speaker visit "Master Rook"
    speaker complete "Master Rook"
    on offer
        conversation
            `A French sailmaker named Celine lays a child's wooden shuttle on the counter. "My apprentice has run off. He is not a child, mind, but he is young enough to think every hard word is a declaration of war."`
            `"His uncle runs a loft in Port Azure. I think he went there, but he has no money for a passage and too much pride to ask. Take this shuttle. He will know it came from me. Tell him the loft door is still open."`
            choice
                `"I'll find him and pass on the message."`
                    accept
                `"Family quarrels are not my trade."`
                    close
    on accept
        log "Accepted The Sailmaker's Son. Take Celine's shuttle and message to her apprentice's uncle at Port Azure."
    on visit
        conversation
            `Master Rook recognises the shuttle immediately. "The stubborn pup has not shown his face, but he left a note here yesterday. He is in the harbour tavern, working up the nerve to go home."`
            `Rook sends a runner to fetch him. The young apprentice arrives looking sheepish, and reads Celine's message twice.`
    on complete
        conversation
            `The apprentice agrees to return to Tortuga after a little more training. Master Rook pays you for the passage and asks you to remind Celine that young men sometimes need to sail a little before they learn where home is.`
